    {
      "topLeftX": 123,
      "topLeftY": 135,
      "bottomRightX": 700,
      "bottomRightY": 218,
      "content": "LBPM is defined as a low power signaling mechanism for two SuperSpeedPlus ports to communicate with each other based on LFPS signals. The adoption of Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) is to embed the transmitting clock in data and to allow for easy data recovery at the receiver based on LFPS clock defined in Table 6-28. This section describes the concept and construction of LBPM. Refer to Chapter 7 for use of LBPM.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
